            "props": {
              "markdown": {
                "escapeHtml": false
              },
              "sectionSpacing": 8,
              "source": "\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.55;padding:0 0 16px 0;\"\u003eReconcile one past shift on one press and die against the press sheet in your hand. Every figure on this screen is one of two kinds: \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eRecorded\u003c/span\u003e is what the MES already has on record; \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eActual\u003c/span\u003e is what the sheet says, and it is what you type.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#093240;border-left:5px solid #22A8CC;border-radius:4px;padding:12px 14px;margin:4px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;padding-bottom:4px;\"\u003eNothing is written until you confirm\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eEverything you type, every LOT you add, and every entry you re-file to another shift stays on this screen only, until you say so. Pressing \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eReview \u0026 Save\u003c/span\u003e at the bottom writes nothing by itself \u0026ndash; see the last step below for what it actually does. \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eDiscard\u003c/span\u003e at any point discards the whole sheet with no trace left behind.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e1\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eCheck the banner\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eIt names the exact \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eshift\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003epress\u003c/span\u003e and \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003edie\u003c/span\u003e you are reconciling \u0026ndash; plus current die life. If any of the three is wrong, use \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eAll shifts\u003c/span\u003e below to go back and pick again.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eThe line under the banner names who this save will be credited to \u0026ndash; that is not decorative.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e2\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eSay why you are here\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003ePick a \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eReason\u003c/span\u003e for the reconciliation. Some reasons ask for a short note as well \u0026ndash; the note field only appears when the reason you picked needs one.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eIf nothing was ever recorded for this shift at all, the screen says so directly instead of looking broken. Everything from there on comes straight off the press sheet.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e3\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eType the shift totals\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eUnder \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eShift totals\u003c/span\u003e, enter \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eTotal shots\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eGood shots\u003c/span\u003e and \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eWarm-up shots\u003c/span\u003e straight off the sheet. Each row shows what is already \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eRecorded\u003c/span\u003e beside what you type as \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eActual\u003c/span\u003e, and a \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eGap\u003c/span\u003e that turns green the moment the two agree.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eTotal shots has to equal good shots plus warm-up shots. If it does not, Save tells you which figure looks wrong, not just that something does not add up.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#093240;border-left:5px solid #22A8CC;border-radius:4px;padding:12px 14px;margin:4px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;padding-bottom:4px;\"\u003eWhy the numbers have to add up\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eTotal good pieces\u003c/span\u003e and \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eNo-good pieces\u003c/span\u003e are not boxes you fill in yourself \u0026ndash; the screen works them out: good shots times the die\u0027s active cavities, less whatever no-good you log below. That worked-out figure is what every LOT\u0027s \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eActual\u003c/span\u003e has to add up to before Save will go through \u0026ndash; which is also why a shift with LOTs still missing cannot be saved until every LTT from the sheet has been entered.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e4\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eLog any no-good pieces\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eAdd a \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003e+ Reject line\u003c/span\u003e for each one: pick the \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eReason\u003c/span\u003e and the \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eAmt\u003c/span\u003e, and \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eApproved by (QAS)\u003c/span\u003e if it was approved by QAS. These are what the screen subtracts to work out Total good pieces above.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e5\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eAdd the LTTs from the press sheet\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eUnder \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eLOTs on this die\u003c/span\u003e, scan or type each \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eLTT\u003c/span\u003e off the ticket, one at a time, then press \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003e+ Add LTT\u003c/span\u003e. LTTs are shared across the whole die building, so consecutive numbers say nothing about which press or shift used them.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eA brand-new LTT is created and released the moment you add it here \u0026ndash; you do not have to wait for Save for it to exist.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#3A2E10;border-left:5px solid #F4B343;border-radius:4px;padding:12px 14px;margin:4px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;padding-bottom:4px;\"\u003eIf an LTT is refused\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eEvery LTT is checked the instant you enter it, not when you save, so you find out with the LOT still in your hand. It is refused when it belongs to another press or die (the message names which one), when it is not a die cast LOT at all (it is some other part elsewhere in the plant), or when it is not a valid LTT (an LTT is 8 or 9 digits). An LTT already on this die is not a refusal \u0026ndash; it just adds to that LOT.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e6\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eEnter what actually landed on each LOT\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eType the piece count from the sheet into that LOT\u0027s \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eActual\u003c/span\u003e box. What is already \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eRecorded\u003c/span\u003e sits right next to it, so you can see the difference as you type.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#093240;border-left:5px solid #22A8CC;border-radius:4px;padding:12px 14px;margin:4px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;padding-bottom:4px;\"\u003eWhen a LOT\u0027s count stands\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eOnce a LOT has been counted at Trim, or its count has already been corrected once, its \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eActual\u003c/span\u003e box locks and says why \u0026ndash; something like \u0026ldquo;Counted at Trim 14:22\u0026rdquo;. That number is what goes forward: a reconciliation still records the shift\u0027s production against that LOT, it just leaves the count itself alone.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e7\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eRe-file an entry on the wrong shift\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eIf \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eEntries on record\u003c/span\u003e shows something that was recorded against the wrong shift, open it and pick the shift it actually happened on. \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eShots, pieces, LOTs and die life\u003c/span\u003e do not change \u0026ndash; only which shift is credited.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"border-top:1px solid #172238;margin:2px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e8\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eReview, then Save\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003ePress \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eReview \u0026 Save\u003c/span\u003e. It runs every check the save will and opens a confirmation panel laying out exactly what would change \u0026ndash; pieces added, pieces removed, new LOTs, counts corrected, counts left standing, die life before and after. Only pressing \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eSAVE\u003c/span\u003e inside that panel commits it.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eReview \u0026 Save\u003c/span\u003e stays disabled while anything still needs fixing, and the label on it says how many \u0026ndash; never that the totals do not match, because fixing that is filling in a number, not forcing one.\u003c/div\u003e",
              "style": {
                "fontSize": 13,
                "overflow": "auto"
              }
            },
            "type": "ia.display.markdown"
          }
        ],
        "meta": {
          "name": "Body"
        },
        "position": {
          "basis": "0px",
          "grow": 1
        },
        "props": {
          "direction": "column",
          "style": {
            "classes": "modal-body"
          }
        },
        "type": "ia.container.flex"
      }
    ],
    "meta": {
      "name": "root"
    },
    "props": {
      "direction": "column",
      "style": {
        "classes": "modal"
      }
    },
    "type": "ia.container.flex"
  }
}
